<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    Smelting (system: crafting.materialladder): ore to metal, metal to alloy. Its own file, per CLAUDE.md. The
    ladder these make up, and why the vein is ore rather than RimWorld's straight-out-of-the-rock steel, is in
    ThingDefs_Items/Items_Metals.xml; the benches are ThingDefs_Buildings/Buildings_Smelting.xml.

    SOURCED: RimWorld's one smelting recipe, ExtractMetalFromSlag (Core Recipes_Production.xml, read): one slag
    chunk to 15 Steel, workAmount 400, no workSkill, worked at the ElectricSmelter. Smelt_Steel is that recipe
    with ore where the slag was — same 400, same 15, same bench — and every recipe here follows it in having
    no workSkill.

    UNSOURCED (no RimWorld recipe exists to read): every other amount. What is deliberate is the shape —
      - each era's metal costs more ore and more work than the last made it (copper 15 ore and 400, iron 20
        and 800, cementation steel a further 1200 on top of the iron);
      - tin bronze is nine parts copper to one of tin, the historical alloy;
      - arsenical bronze needs no tin but wastes ore (25 for 10), so a settlement with tin prefers tin bronze
        and one without still reaches the bronze age — tin is the rarest vein on the map
        (Buildings_Mineable.xml), and RimWorld has no tin at all;
      - the electric smelter is the cheapest steel there is, which is what an industrial revolution is.
    Crafting.SmeltingInitiative picks between two recipes for one metal by newest research first and then by
    metal out per unit in; the tests pin those choices, never these numbers.

    NOT PORTED: ChunkSlagSteel. RimWorld's slag comes from the wrecks a crashed colony lands among; this game
    has no wreck to scatter it, and a smelting byproduct nothing on the map would ever use was colony detail
    that serves no era. Recorded in docs/status.json.
  -->

  <RecipeDef>
    <defName>Smelt_Copper</defName>
    <researchPrerequisites>
      <li>Copper</li>
    </researchPrerequisites>
    <label>smelt copper</label>
    <jobString>Smelting copper.</jobString>
    <workAmount>400</workAmount>
    <ingredients>
      <li>
        <filter><thingDefs><li>CopperOre</li></thingDefs></filter>
        <count>15</count>
      </li>
    </ingredients>
    <products><Copper>10</Copper></products>
    <recipeUsers><li>SmeltingFurnace</li><li>Bloomery</li><li>ElectricSmelter</li></recipeUsers>
  </RecipeDef>

  <RecipeDef>
    <defName>Make_Bronze</defName>
    <researchPrerequisites>
      <li>Bronze</li>
    </researchPrerequisites>
    <label>cast bronze</label>
    <jobString>Casting bronze.</jobString>
    <workAmount>400</workAmount>
    <ingredients>
      <li>
        <filter><thingDefs><li>Copper</li></thingDefs></filter>
        <count>9</count>
      </li>
      <li>
        <filter><thingDefs><li>Tin</li></thingDefs></filter>
        <count>1</count>
      </li>
    </ingredients>
    <products><Bronze>10</Bronze></products>
    <recipeUsers><li>SmeltingFurnace</li><li>Bloomery</li></recipeUsers>
  </RecipeDef>

  <RecipeDef>
    <defName>Make_Bronze_Arsenical</defName>
    <researchPrerequisites>
      <li>Bronze</li>
    </researchPrerequisites>
    <label>smelt arsenical bronze</label>
    <jobString>Smelting arsenical bronze.</jobString>
    <workAmount>600</workAmount>
    <ingredients>
      <li>
        <filter><thingDefs><li>CopperOre</li></thingDefs></filter>
        <count>25</count>
      </li>
    </ingredients>
    <products><Bronze>10</Bronze></products>
    <recipeUsers><li>SmeltingFurnace</li><li>Bloomery</li></recipeUsers>
  </RecipeDef>

  <RecipeDef>
    <defName>Smelt_Iron</defName>
    <researchPrerequisites>
      <li>Iron</li>
    </researchPrerequisites>
    <label>smelt iron</label>
    <jobString>Smelting iron.</jobString>
    <workAmount>800</workAmount>
    <ingredients>
      <li>
        <filter><thingDefs><li>IronOre</li></thingDefs></filter>
        <count>20</count>
      </li>
    </ingredients>
    <products><Iron>10</Iron></products>
    <recipeUsers><li>Bloomery</li><li>ElectricSmelter</li></recipeUsers>
  </RecipeDef>

  <RecipeDef>
    <defName>Make_Steel_Cementation</defName>
    <researchPrerequisites>
      <li>Steel</li>
    </researchPrerequisites>
    <label>make cementation steel</label>
    <jobString>Making steel.</jobString>
    <workAmount>1200</workAmount>
    <ingredients>
      <li>
        <filter><thingDefs><li>Iron</li></thingDefs></filter>
        <count>10</count>
      </li>
    </ingredients>
    <products><Steel>8</Steel></products>
    <recipeUsers><li>Bloomery</li></recipeUsers>
  </RecipeDef>

  <RecipeDef>
    <defName>Smelt_Steel</defName>
    <researchPrerequisites>
      <li>Electricity</li>
    </researchPrerequisites>
    <label>smelt steel</label>
    <jobString>Smelting steel.</jobString>
    <workAmount>400</workAmount>
    <ingredients>
      <li>
        <filter><thingDefs><li>IronOre</li></thingDefs></filter>
        <count>20</count>
      </li>
    </ingredients>
    <products><Steel>15</Steel></products>
    <recipeUsers><li>ElectricSmelter</li></recipeUsers>
  </RecipeDef>

</Defs>
